# select-once returns [Result.Ok v] on successful receive
# Phase 3: select-once protocol redesign (T-810)
#
# Strategy: force send before select-once by making result depend on sent.
# [if [= sent []] ...] forces the send call (send returns []), then select-once runs.
# Sources use {ch: handler:} dict format. The channel value is never serialized —
# only %.result (a Variant) is accessed in doc 2.
# Multi-doc pipeline: doc 1 returns the computation dict; doc 2 matches.
--- uses: ["core"]
[
  ch: [channel 10]
  sent: [send ch 42]
  sources: [seq [{ch: ch  handler: [fn [let v] v]}] [builtin-variant "Seq.Nil"]]
  result: [if [= sent []] [select-once [context] sources] [select-once [context] sources]]
]
---
[match %.result
  [case [let v] [Result.Ok v] v]
  Closed.Closed: -1]
=== out
Int(42)
